PARSFILE
#FullDataName Control: Speed (Closed Loop) Using Path Preview`0.2/0.2 G Max Ax/Ay Limits, 100 km/h max`Highway Driving
INSTALL_DRIVER_SPEED_CONTROLLER CarSim9
#RingCtrl0 2
OPT_SC_SKILL 2
#RingCtrl1 1
#RingCtrl2 1
#RingCtrl3 1
#RingCtrl4 1
#RingCtrl5 1
SPEED_TARGET_COMBINE ADD
SPEED_TARGET_CONSTANT 0
SPEED_AX_THROTTLE_CONSTANT 0.2
SPEED_AX_BRAKE_CONSTANT 0.2
SPEED_AY_LEFT_CONSTANT 0.2
SPEED_AY_RIGHT_CONSTANT 0.2
SPEED_TARGET_S_CONSTANT 100
OPT_SC 4
#CheckBox0 1    
OPT_SC_ENGINE_BRAKING 1
#CheckBox1 0    
#CheckBox2 0    
OPT_SC_3D 0

SPEED_KP 0.15
SPEED_KI 0.1
SPEED_KP3 0
BK_PERF_SC 0.1
FPD_PERF_SC 0.1
SPEED_PREVIEW_STEP 4
SPEED_CURV_LENGTH 8
SPEED_PREVIEW_START 0
SPEED_PREVIEW 100
PBK_CON_MAX_SC 10

#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#In daily highway driving drivers limit themselves to fairly low acceleration levels. Here we use a maximum of 0.2 G's in all directions.
#
#The speed is expected to be largely constant, so there is some integral gain to cause the controller to converge on the right speed.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: Control: Speed (Closed Loop) Using Path Preview; { Highway Driving } 0.2/0.2 G Max Ax/Ay Limits, 100 km/h max
#Library : Control: Speed (Closed Loop) Using Path Preview
#DataSet : 0.2/0.2 G Max Ax/Ay Limits, 100 km/h max
#Category: Highway Driving
#FileID  : SpdPath_b525f579-b67b-4db2-8cca-9d4215c6901d
#Product : CarSim 2017.1
#VehCode Speed Using Path Preview

END
